stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB

    state "DRAFT - generated or edited, not approved" as DRAFT
    state "APPROVED - named approver and date recorded" as APPROVED
    state "PUBLISHED - live, with publication evidence" as PUBLISHED
    state "STALE - published, but the configuration it describes has changed" as STALE
    state "SUPERSEDED - replaced by a later published version" as SUPERSEDED
    state "DISCARDED - draft abandoned" as DISCARDED

    [*] --> DRAFT: Establishment created, or a staleness trigger opens the next version
    DRAFT --> DISCARDED: Abandoned
    DRAFT --> APPROVED: Named approval, every required Rule 8 clause filled
    APPROVED --> PUBLISHED: Publication evidence recorded, website URL or dated premises attestation
    PUBLISHED --> STALE: Talent AI or confirmer configuration changed, liaison officer vacated, URL unreachable, or attestation aged out
    PUBLISHED --> SUPERSEDED: A later version publishes
    STALE --> SUPERSEDED: A later version publishes
    STALE --> DRAFT: Tenant starts the next version
    SUPERSEDED --> [*]
    DISCARDED --> [*]

    note right of PUBLISHED
        Content set by size: at twenty or more employees the full
        Rule 8 clause 3 content including the manner of selection
        and the liaison officer. Below twenty, facilities and
        amenities only. Publication binds every establishment.
    end note

    note right of STALE
        Staleness is shown to the tenant, never silently corrected
        by editing a document already published. Falling below
        twenty employees never downgrades a published version.
    end note

    note right of SUPERSEDED
        Registration with the Chief or State Commissioner is
        correspondence, not a portal: prepare, dispatch, acknowledge
        or resubmit, outcome. The word registered appears only
        against a recorded acknowledgement.
    end note
